# Rules in this file describe *this repository's own* files. Two shapes are safe:
# anchored to the root (`/build/`), or directory-scoped with a middle slash
# (`.edgeone/*` — git anchors those too). Everything else also matches paths
# *inside* `market-source/`, which is mirrored market payload: the sync copies
# it and lists it in `_files.txt`, git then silently refuses to commit it, and
# every client that mirrors the listing gets a 404 — invisible on the machine
# that ran the sync, because its disk still has the file. Exclusions for the
# market tree belong in `scripts/sync-market-tree.mjs` (keep the two in step).
# `bun run check:market` guards this with probes; that is what `ignore.market-tree`
# reports. Never add an unanchored directory name or a bare `*.ext` glob.

# React Router generated types/cache
/.react-router/

# Build output (React Router SSG → static files)
/build/

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Market tree is committed on purpose — but since doc 30 it is the **packing
# input**, not what the site serves: the three markets ship as zip archives on
# ModelScope (`scripts/pack-market-zips.mjs` packs them, `scripts/publish-market-zips.mjs`
# uploads them), and only the catalog-page icons still reach the build output.
# It lives outside `public/` (Vite would copy it during the build and stall
# prerender) and is copied into the output by scripts/copy-market-tree.mjs —
# see scripts/sync-market-tree.mjs.

# Release artifacts (zips are built per release by scripts/release.mjs and
# uploaded to GitHub Releases; never commit them)
/dist-release/

# Market archives (built by `bun run pack:market`, uploaded by
# `bun run publish:market`; the recorded digests live in content/market-hosts.json)
/dist-market/

# Logs — the dev server writes dev.log / dev.err / dev-server.log at the root.
# Anchored: an unanchored `*.log` also matches a payload file inside the market
# tree. A market payload *may* ship its own logs; the dependency is on the sync's
# exclusions, not on these rules.
/*.log
/*.err

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db


# The IDE's own project folder. This rule was unanchored until 2026-09-17 and
# cost the experts market 84 payload files, exactly as the header describes.
/.codebuddy/

# Tencent Cloud EdgeOne
.env
.edgeone/*
.tef_dist/*

# Deliberately global, unlike the rules above — each one keeps its market-tree
# counterpart in `scripts/sync-market-tree.mjs`, so nothing is listed that git
# would refuse:
#   node_modules/        — npm creates it at any depth; DEEP_EXCLUDES agrees
#   .DS_Store, Thumbs.db — OS junk; FILE_EXCLUDES agrees
#   .env above           — secret hygiene outranks market fidelity. If a payload
#                          ever ships one, `ignore.market-tree` reports it rather
#                          than dropping it silently.
